  "caveats": [
    "Sampling is targeted, not random: inspectors favour symptomatic trees and the buffer and containment zones, and stop sampling once an area is declared infected.",
    "Cells the scanner never judges (built-up land, non-WorldCover classes) count as not flagged, because state.npz does not store the land mask.",
    "Outside the infected zone, positive trees must be removed, and in eradication areas also the host plants within 50 m (Reg. (EU) 2020/1201, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2020/1201/oj). Removal looks like decline to the scanner. A flag in the season after a positive (lag 1) may show the eradication rather than the disease.",
    "About a third of positives had no symptoms; no canopy-based method can see those.",
    "Coordinates are those recorded by the inspectors; a tree near a cell edge may be matched to the wrong cell, which the 3 x 3 window only partly absorbs."
  ]
}
